' ============================================================================
' Manilov__ForwardJumpSequence__ELI5.puml
'
' Purpose : Plain-language companion to Manilov__ForwardJumpSequence.puml.
'           Same two-checkpoint story, no packet-filter internals.
' Source  : docs/adr/0006-ManilovNetworkOwnership.md - D4, D4a, section 6b (OQ5).
' Scope   : Exactly five ideas: two checkpoints in a row; door one can only
'           stop; desk two defaults to stop; the permit is read at desk two
'           before any guard step that can end the queue; placed after that
'           guard step, the permit is never read and the visitor vanishes
'           silently.
' Note    : Deliberately jargon-free. Do not add rule-engine terms here; put
'           them in the technical diagram instead.
' Render  : plantuml -tpng -tsvg docs/_diagrams/Manilov__ForwardJumpSequence__ELI5.puml
' ============================================================================

@startuml
title Two checkpoints, two orders — plain view

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #F7FBFF
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

rectangle "GOOD ORDER" as GOOD #EAF7EA {
  rectangle "Visitor arrives" as G1
  rectangle "Inner door (check 1 of 2):\nlocks only, never opens" as G2
  rectangle "Front desk (check 2 of 2), default no:\nread the visitor pass FIRST" as G3
  rectangle "Waved through;\nthe 'no appointment' step never runs" as G4
  G1 --> G2
  G2 --> G3
  G3 --> G4
}

rectangle "BAD ORDER" as BAD #FDECEC {
  rectangle "Visitor arrives" as B1
  rectangle "Inner door (check 1 of 2):\nlocks only, never opens" as B2
  rectangle "Front desk (check 2 of 2), default no:\n'no appointment → leave' runs first" as B3
  rectangle "Gone before the pass is read.\nSilent — no error is shown." as B4
  B1 --> B2
  B2 --> B3
  B3 --> B4
}

GOOD -[hidden]right- BAD
note bottom of G4
Good order: the pass is read at the front desk,
so the visitor is let through.
end note

note bottom of B4
Bad order: the guard ends the queue before the pass is read;
the visitor disappears and nothing reports it.
end note

legend right
|= In the building |= On the packet path |
| Visitor | one packet |
| Inner door (locks only) | VM-side check: can only say "stop" |
| Front desk (default: no visitors) | host-side check: default is "stop" |
| Visitor pass | the "let this through" slip |
| Guard: "no appointment → leave" | any guard step that can end the queue |
| Waved through | packet continues |
| Gone, no error | packet stopped silently |
endlegend

@enduml
